    "body": "If I add these lines before setting `frame.src`:\r\n```\r\nsetTimeout(\"console.log('timer')\", 0);\r\nPromise.resolve().then(() => console.log(\"promise\"));\r\n```\r\nI get `load`, `promise`, `beforeunload`, `timer`, `unload`, `load` reliably in Chrome. In Safari however I sometimes (rarely though) get the `timer` before `beforeunload`. (If I add another `Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log(\"promise\"));` after setting `frame.src` it will still log before `beforeunload` reliably.)\r\n\r\n(Also somewhat weird. Sometimes when I refresh in Firefox (and also sometimes in Chrome for `unload` only) it logs `beforeunload` and `unload` events first.\r\n\r\nI suspect we need @cdumez @rbyers (not sure who to ask from Chrome) to help us out here.",
